cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SO3C: Lorentz-covariant jet tagging with complexified-SO(3) geodesic flows"
abstract: "Jet taggers built on the complexified rotation algebra so(3) + i so(3) = so(3,C), which is isomorphic to the Lorentz algebra so(3,1). Each constituent is lifted to a complex 3-vector relative to the jet and moved along the closed-form flow z' = -[a] x z by a learned covariant connection; the flow conserves the bilinear invariant z.z and is evaluated with a complex Rodrigues formula, so no ODE solver is involved. The message-passing model runs several such rounds with an invariant scalar channel; optional beam particles reduce the symmetry to rotations about the beam axis while the model stays exactly covariant when the beams are transformed with the jet. On the Kasieczka top-tagging reference dataset a 22,834-parameter model reaches AUC 0.9839 and background rejection 1202 at 30% signal efficiency (single run; an ensemble of five models, three 30-epoch seeds plus the 60- and 120-epoch snapshots of a fourth run, reaches 0.9841 and 1270), below the best published Lorentz-symmetric taggers (PELICAN 0.9870 and 2250). Includes the benchmark harness, the Kaggle notebooks, the result files behind the reported GPU results and the checkpoints of the headline models."
